The Chimaera Project is pleased to announce the public release of
version 0.9.2 of aterr, an open source threaded forum system.

Version 0.9.2 of aterr fixes problems with installing aterr to the root
of a domain, and includes some new minor functionality such as thread
pagination and limiting the effectiveness of forum/SEO spam.

aterr is a threaded forum system, allowing registered visitors to
express their opinions,  discuss topics, and debate with other
visitors. A threaded forum system differs from regular, flat forum
systems in that once posted, a thread can fork, allowing visitors to
reply directly to other posts. aterr also provides a customisable
permissions system, the ability to nest forums, and moderation tools.

aterr can be downloaded from:
 --> http://chimaera.starglade.org/aterr/aterr-0.9.2.tar.gz

A demonstration site, as well as the official support forums, is at:
 --> http://chimaera.starglade.org/forums/

aterr is released under the GNU GPL.

Chris

