DemoRecorder-2.5alpha9a is now available at http://www.DemoRecorder.com
Release Date: March 19, 2006

Changes in this Release:

     * Added the following options to demorec-to-flv,
       the FLV export filter (FLV is Flash Video for Web publishing):

	--autoplay
		the exported video starts playing automatically	

	--autorepeat
                 the exported video repeats playback after it reached
                 the end of the video.

         --controller-mode mode
                 sets the mode of the controller-GUI of the player.
                 mode can be one of
                         on     switches on the GUI for controlling the player
                         off    switches off the GUI for controlling the player
                         auto   the GUI is only completely visible when
                                    the mouse moves over it.
                         none   there is no GUI, just the movie is displayed
		
     * Added the following options to all export filters:

	--start, --end:
		select part of the video for exporting
		by specifying start-time and end-time
		relative to the recording.

Description:

	DemoRecorder is a screen recorder for Linux
	with the ability to record sound from the
	microphone which is synchronized to the recorded video.

	A screen recorder is a tool which can record all
	desktop-activity into a movie and it can be used for
	* training of users,
	* augmenting of documentation, howtos, etc
	* marketing of software by explaining what a software can do
	* usability tests
	* ...

	DemoRecorder has export-filters for publising
	* on the Web using Flash technology.
		see also the tutorial:
		http://DemoRecorder.com/howto/easy-web-publishing
	* on Video DVD ( MPEG2 export filter )
	* in AVI-format with MPEG4

	All export filters support exporting the sound
	recorded from the microphone.

	The recording technology of DemoRecorder provides
	the equivalent of high framerates while having
	low CPU requirements. For more info, please read
		http://DemoRecorder.com/info/recording-technology.php

	The export-filter for the Web generates all files
	necessary for Web-publishing, i.e.
	* an html-fragment to copy-paste into the web-page where
	  you want to show the video.
	* an FLV-file containing the video.
	* an SWF-file which contains the loader/player for
	  streaming the FLV-video.

	The video can be played back with any browser having
	the Flash-Player-Plugin Version 7 or later installed
	which is the case for more than 90% of all browser
	installations.

	The FLV-video has to be loaded from a webserver, so
	please test it with your local testing server instead
	of just loading it from the file-system.

DemoRecorder is commercial software
and has a free 30 day evaluation period.

Feedback is welcome and feature wishes
have a good chance to be included into DemoRecorder.

--
Christian Linhart

Christian Linhart Software

